---
name: zotero-paper-updater
description: Maintain existing Zotero paper records, attachments, local PDFs, and related MinerU caches. Use for full-library or single-paper maintenance, metadata completion, proven duplicate cleanup, relationship repair, and Zotero-standard filename synchronization. Do not use for reading, summarizing, comparing, or taking notes on paper content.
---

# Zotero Paper Updater

Maintain existing papers already represented in Zotero or the managed paper directory. Do not import new PDFs or create Zotero parent items.

## Boundaries

- No arguments means maintain the existing library under `E:\paper`.
- `-ItemKey` or `-Path` scopes the same maintenance workflow to one paper.
- Preserve unknown metadata as empty and report it as unresolved.
- Repair only uniquely provable relationships; otherwise report without changing them.
- Permanently remove only strictly proven duplicates, preserving the copy with user records.
- Never edit `zotero.sqlite`.
- Do not read paper content, generate notes, or require a healthy MinerU `full.md` for unrelated maintenance.

## Route

For every supported request, read and follow `workflows/maintain-library.md`.

Other skills must call `scripts/maintain-library.ps1` with `-ItemKey` or `-Path` and consume its JSON result. They must not copy this workflow or call internal scripts.

## Public interface

```powershell
pwsh -NoProfile -File .\scripts\maintain-library.ps1 [-ItemKey <key> | -Path <pdf>] 
```

The command writes one JSON document to stdout. Read `references/result-contract.md` when consuming or changing that contract.

